0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"book":{"id":"holt","title":"Cybercrime and Digital Forensics","authors":"Thomas J. Holt, Adam M. Bossler & Kathryn C. Seigfried-Spellar","publisher":"Routledge","year":"3rd edition · 2022","color":"navy","code":"CRIME / SOCIETY / TECHNOLOGY","url":"https://www.routledge.com/Cybercrime-and-Digital-Forensics-An-Introduction/Holt-Bossler-Seigfried-Spellar/p/book/9780367360078","description":"Start here for the human and social context of cybercrime, then connect offending patterns to investigation and evidence. The third edition contains 17 chapters.","editionNote":"Chapter titles follow the publisher’s third-edition listing. The explanations and study prompts below are original. Indian legal updates come from primary sources, not this 2022 text.","chapters":[{"title":"1. Technology and Cybercrime","summary":"Distinguish computer-target and computer-enabled conduct. Build a vocabulary for actors, systems, and harms before selecting an investigative method.","topics":["1.1","1.5"]},{"title":"2. Law Enforcement, Privacy, and Security in Dealing with Cybercrime","summary":"Compare institutional roles and the tension between investigative access and civil liberties. Translate the discussion into an Indian authority register.","topics":["1.8","2.1","2.3"]},{"title":"3. Computer Hackers and Hacking","summary":"Examine hacking subcultures, authorization, and legal frameworks without treating technical curiosity as a single criminal category.","topics":["1.4","3.8"]},{"title":"4. Malware and Automated Computer Attacks","summary":"Connect malware behavior to observable artifacts and response priorities. Separate the program’s function from attribution to an actor.","topics":["3.8","4.7"]},{"title":"5. Digital Piracy and Intellectual Property Theft","summary":"Study the social and economic organization of unauthorized distribution, and distinguish the relevant legal interests from system intrusion.","topics":["1.4","2.5"]},{"title":"6. Online Fraud","summary":"Trace deception, identity misuse, and payment inducement. Use the invoice case to practice an ingredient table and preservation plan.","topics":["1.5","3.11"]},{"title":"7. Pornography, Image-Based Sexual Abuse, and Prostitution","summary":"Approach image-based harm through victim protection, legal distinctions, and sensitive evidence handling. Do not reproduce or circulate harmful material.","topics":["1.5","2.12"]},{"title":"8. Child Sexual Exploitation Material Offenses","summary":"Understand the specialized legal and safeguarding framework. This course gives conceptual guidance only and contains no exploitative material or operational acquisition instructions.","topics":["1.6","2.12"]},{"title":"9. Cyberbullying, Online Harassment, and Cyberstalking","summary":"Consider repetition, context, harm, and platform records. Compare the general Indian provisions without assuming every offensive post is stalking.","topics":["1.5","3.4"]},{"title":"10. Online Extremism and Cyberterror","summary":"Separate extremist content, mobilization, and the narrower legal definition of terrorist conduct. Identify the evidence needed for intent and effects.","topics":["5.5"]},{"title":"11. Cyberwarfare and Information Operations Online","summary":"Examine state interests, offensive and defensive operations, and information influence while keeping legal thresholds explicit.","topics":["5.4","5.6"]},{"title":"12. Illicit Market Operations Online","summary":"Evaluate market claims, reputation, and transaction trails. Distinguish a public ledger observation from proof of address ownership.","topics":["3.6","5.1"]},{"title":"13. Cybercrime and Criminological Theories","summary":"Use theory to form alternative explanations about offending and victimization, not to infer guilt from a profile.","topics":["1.3","5.3"]},{"title":"14. Evolution of Digital Forensics","summary":"Connect the growth of digital evidence to method, process models, and the examiner’s responsibilities.","topics":["2.4","3.7"]},{"title":"15. Acquisition and Examination of Forensic Evidence","summary":"Study preservation, imaging, examination, and reporting. Practise the integrity workflow, then update the legal references to the BSA.","topics":["2.6","4.4","4.5"]},{"title":"16. Legal Challenges in Digital Forensic Investigations","summary":"Compare constitutional, admissibility, and expert-evidence issues. The book’s international treatment must be supplemented with current Indian law.","topics":["2.9","2.10","4.12"]},{"title":"17. The Future of Cybercrime, Terror, and Policy","summary":"Evaluate emerging technologies through scenarios, uncertainty, and policy choices rather than prediction alone.","topics":["5.7","5.12"]}]}}],["$L3"],"$L4"]}],"isPartial":false,"staleTime":300,"varyParams":null,"buildId":"mMiCr23A_-Cpk0hZkfT7X"}
